    "question": {
      ":question/id": "55cecc39-f460-5ecf-abe4-4ef195040d31",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in [0,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-2,2]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it is one-to-one on that interval.\n\nThe function is constant: distinct inputs in each listed interval have the same output $2$. Thus it is not one-to-one on any of the three intervals.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of these intervals\".",
